1
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:04,546
PARK MINJAE'S LIST

2
00:00:04,630 --> 00:00:05,923
START DATING...

3
00:00:36,620 --> 00:00:40,958
BETWEEN STEPS

4
00:00:41,625 --> 00:00:43,835
CHARACTERS, PLACES, ORGANIZATIONS,
AND EVENTS IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

5
00:00:43,919 --> 00:00:45,504
THIS DRAMA CONTAINS SENSITIVE CONTENT

6
00:00:47,005 --> 00:00:49,216
EPISODE 7

7
00:00:56,223 --> 00:00:58,475
-Subin, would you like some fried rice?
-Yeah.

8
00:00:59,893 --> 00:01:01,395
-[Youjin] This much?
-Yeah.

9
00:01:07,192 --> 00:01:08,360
-You want salmon?
-Yeah.

10
00:01:08,443 --> 00:01:10,279
-Salmon's nice.
-I'm going to have some.

11
00:01:10,362 --> 00:01:11,822
[Youjin] I'll take the squid.

12
00:01:13,156 --> 00:01:14,950
-Do you want some salmon?
-Just a piece.

13
00:01:23,292 --> 00:01:24,543
[in English] Thank you.

14
00:01:39,016 --> 00:01:40,601
-Enjoy.
-Thanks.

15
00:01:41,101 --> 00:01:42,102
Enjoy, everyone.

16
00:01:42,728 --> 00:01:44,813
Here, help yourself.

17
00:01:44,896 --> 00:01:46,398
-Thank you.
-Sure.

18
00:01:46,940 --> 00:01:48,358
Just relax and enjoy your food.

19
00:01:53,196 --> 00:01:54,489
-You know what?
-Yeah?

20
00:01:54,573 --> 00:01:56,283
-I'll treat you next time.
-Nah.

21
00:01:57,117 --> 00:01:59,661
There's a new place near campus
that has amazing tiramisu.

22
00:01:59,745 --> 00:02:01,705
Tiramishu? I love tiramishu.

23
00:02:02,205 --> 00:02:03,248
[Chansoo] "Tiramishu?"

24
00:02:03,332 --> 00:02:05,250
What's that? Is it something tasty?

25
00:02:06,043 --> 00:02:08,378
Tiramishu is a kind of pastry.

26
00:02:09,254 --> 00:02:11,256
Didn't you know that?

27
00:02:11,340 --> 00:02:13,717
It's not a pastry. It's a cake.

28
00:02:14,843 --> 00:02:17,763
So, to be precise,

29
00:02:17,846 --> 00:02:20,015
it's not "tiramishu."

30
00:02:20,098 --> 00:02:22,559
It's "su." [chuckles]

31
00:02:22,643 --> 00:02:24,603
It's Italian, "tiramisu."

32
00:02:24,686 --> 00:02:25,687
Oh.

33
00:02:26,104 --> 00:02:28,982
You see, it's a traditional Italian cake.

34
00:02:29,066 --> 00:02:31,526
You know, in <i>Italiano.</i>

35
00:02:32,027 --> 00:02:33,028
"Tiramisu."

36
00:02:34,738 --> 00:02:35,739
Oh...

37
00:02:35,822 --> 00:02:37,324
[chuckling] It's nothing.

38
00:02:38,075 --> 00:02:42,454
So, Subin, you like tiramisu?

39
00:02:42,537 --> 00:02:43,705
I love it too.

40
00:02:43,789 --> 00:02:45,666
-Yes.
-[Subin chuckles awkwardly]

41
00:02:45,749 --> 00:02:48,752
Actually, since we're on the subject,

42
00:02:48,835 --> 00:02:50,796
why don't we go try it today?
Are you free?

43
00:02:52,089 --> 00:02:54,091
I don't think I can today.

44
00:02:54,174 --> 00:02:56,051
I need to get back to work.

45
00:02:57,386 --> 00:02:59,680
You're busy even on the weekend, huh?

46
00:02:59,763 --> 00:03:01,807
What time will you be done?

47
00:03:01,890 --> 00:03:04,685
Let's go when you're done.
What time do you finish?

48
00:03:04,768 --> 00:03:07,688
Ah. I'm not sure yet.

49
00:03:07,771 --> 00:03:08,772
[Taeho] I see.

50
00:03:15,946 --> 00:03:16,947
[Minjae] Hmm?

51
00:03:17,406 --> 00:03:19,700
-Where did you get the orange juice?
-This?

52
00:03:19,783 --> 00:03:22,411
Next to the soda fountain.
Should I get you some?

53
00:03:23,370 --> 00:03:24,371
I'll go get it myself.

54
00:03:25,288 --> 00:03:26,289
No, I can go get it.

55
00:03:26,373 --> 00:03:28,458
-Subin, do you want some juice too?
-Yeah, sure.

56
00:03:28,542 --> 00:03:30,919
-[Minjae] I'll get you some.
-[Hangyeol] Don't. I'll go get it.

57
00:03:31,753 --> 00:03:33,463
-I'll go get it.
-No, I'll go get it.

58
00:03:33,547 --> 00:03:35,674
-I can go get it.
-What? No, I'll go get it.

59
00:03:35,757 --> 00:03:37,050
Come on, don't be like that.

60
00:03:37,134 --> 00:03:38,176
What are you doing?

61
00:03:38,260 --> 00:03:39,344
I can go get it myself.

62
00:03:39,428 --> 00:03:40,429
[Hangyeol] No.

63
00:03:44,349 --> 00:03:47,018
My lab mates are all really nice.

64
00:03:47,102 --> 00:03:48,103
Oh.

65
00:03:48,186 --> 00:03:50,439
-Yeah.
-They're all really nice.

66
00:03:51,022 --> 00:03:52,107
Oh...

67
00:03:52,190 --> 00:03:55,735
Ah. Minjae, I wonder
if she's at the airport by now.

68
00:03:56,319 --> 00:03:58,113
I think so. She must have.

69
00:03:58,697 --> 00:04:01,241
Right, why did they change their honeymoon
from Hawaii to Phuket?

70
00:04:01,324 --> 00:04:03,452
They both work full-time.
They don't have time.

71
00:04:03,952 --> 00:04:06,788
Still, you only get to go
on your honeymoon once.

72
00:04:07,831 --> 00:04:09,624
-Here. Orange juice.
-Oh!

73
00:04:09,708 --> 00:04:11,209
-Thank you.
-[chuckles]

74
00:04:15,005 --> 00:04:16,256
Thank you. Let me...

75
00:04:17,382 --> 00:04:18,800
-It's grape juice.
-Oh.

76
00:04:19,801 --> 00:04:20,802
Ah...

77
00:04:20,886 --> 00:04:22,554
Okay. Thank you.

78
00:04:26,224 --> 00:04:27,601
-Which one do you want?
-[Minjae] Here.

79
00:04:27,684 --> 00:04:29,436
-I...
-[Minjae] Drink this. Here.

80
00:04:31,146 --> 00:04:33,064
-No, I'm fine.
-[Youjin] You can have both.

81
00:04:33,148 --> 00:04:35,650
-No, I'm fine.
-No, you should drink it.

82
00:04:38,487 --> 00:04:40,322
-Huh?
-[phone vibrating]

83
00:04:40,405 --> 00:04:41,656
I'll be right back.

84
00:04:42,491 --> 00:04:43,617
Yes, Professor.

85
00:04:45,744 --> 00:04:47,746
-[Sejin coughing]
-Yes.

86
00:04:47,829 --> 00:04:50,123
I just stepped out to grab a bite.

87
00:04:51,249 --> 00:04:52,250
-Yes.
-What's up?

88
00:04:52,334 --> 00:04:54,002
Okay, I will. Bye.

89
00:04:55,837 --> 00:04:57,589
I'm sorry, but I need to head out now.

90
00:04:58,215 --> 00:04:59,257
[Youjin] Okay, bye.

91
00:04:59,341 --> 00:05:00,342
-[Subin] Sorry.
-But...

92
00:05:00,425 --> 00:05:01,426
-Take care.
-But...

93
00:05:02,385 --> 00:05:05,180
-Wait.
-Well, I'll see you next time. I'm sorry.

94
00:05:05,263 --> 00:05:06,932
-[Chansoo] Wait...
-[Hangyeol] What time do you get off?

95
00:05:07,766 --> 00:05:08,850
What time do you...

96
00:05:09,476 --> 00:05:10,894
[Youjin] Come on, for God's sake.

97
00:05:15,565 --> 00:05:18,318
Hey, since it's the weekend
and we're all here,

98
00:05:18,401 --> 00:05:21,530
how about we go grab a beer or something?
What do you say?

99
00:05:21,613 --> 00:05:22,614
-Then...
-Yeah?

100
00:05:22,697 --> 00:05:25,283
There's this new dessert place
that has amazing tiramisu.

101
00:05:25,367 --> 00:05:26,827
Hmm.

102
00:05:26,910 --> 00:05:28,703
Then, shall we go
get some coffee and cake?

103
00:05:28,787 --> 00:05:30,580
Hold on a second. [grunts]

104
00:05:32,082 --> 00:05:34,251
I wonder if the baseball game has begun.

105
00:05:34,334 --> 00:05:35,418
I'll watch the game, then.

106
00:05:35,502 --> 00:05:37,712
Yeah. Hey, put it on.
It has already started.

107
00:05:38,380 --> 00:05:39,548
I'll just watch the game.

108
00:05:40,131 --> 00:05:42,092
-[Chansoo] All right.
-[Taeho] Okay.

109
00:05:42,175 --> 00:05:44,553
-You... You good? All right.
-[Sejin] Yes?

110
00:05:47,889 --> 00:05:49,057
Look here.

111
00:05:49,140 --> 00:05:51,351
-Don't take my picture. [chuckles]
-Come on.

112
00:05:51,434 --> 00:05:52,853
Could you turn your head a little bit?

113
00:05:53,395 --> 00:05:55,814
-No, I don't want to.
-But you look great on camera.

114
00:05:55,897 --> 00:05:56,898
Okay, fine.

115
00:06:01,152 --> 00:06:02,153
You took it, right?

116
00:06:03,321 --> 00:06:04,614
Now, I'll try this.

117
00:06:10,245 --> 00:06:11,580
Mmm!

118
00:06:11,663 --> 00:06:12,664
It's good.

119
00:06:12,747 --> 00:06:14,165
-It's good, right?
-Mmm.

120
00:06:14,249 --> 00:06:15,292
Try this too.

121
00:06:15,375 --> 00:06:16,918
Okay. Sejin, do you want to try?

122
00:06:17,419 --> 00:06:19,379
No, I don't have a sweet tooth.

123
00:06:19,462 --> 00:06:20,463
[Minjae] You don't?

124
00:06:21,298 --> 00:06:23,300
If so, why did you follow us here?

125
00:06:24,634 --> 00:06:27,262
No, it's actually not as sweet
as you think. Try it.

126
00:06:28,263 --> 00:06:29,264
Come on, try it.

127
00:06:33,393 --> 00:06:34,603
Mmm.

128
00:06:34,686 --> 00:06:36,479
It's not bad. It's delicious.

129
00:06:41,776 --> 00:06:44,112
How about we go to the movies?
It's been a while.

130
00:06:44,613 --> 00:06:45,822
Anything you've been wanting to see?

131
00:06:46,615 --> 00:06:47,741
[Youjin] Hmm...

132
00:06:47,824 --> 00:06:49,200
I'm okay with anything.

133
00:06:49,701 --> 00:06:51,494
What should we see?

134
00:06:51,578 --> 00:06:53,830
It's the weekend,
so there may be no tickets left.

135
00:06:53,913 --> 00:06:56,499
-Let me look it up.
-Yeah, look it up.

136
00:06:58,877 --> 00:07:01,421
Action or adventure? What do you think?

137
00:07:01,504 --> 00:07:03,173
That looks good. Something light.

138
00:07:04,382 --> 00:07:07,510
How about this? I heard it's really fun.
It's got good ratings too.

139
00:07:08,053 --> 00:07:10,430
I don't really like the poster.
Is there anything else?

140
00:07:10,513 --> 00:07:12,474
Then, are you more into
this kind of thing?

141
00:07:12,557 --> 00:07:15,477
That's a little... It's an animated movie.

142
00:07:15,977 --> 00:07:17,395
I should get going.

143
00:07:17,479 --> 00:07:19,022
I need to go home.

144
00:07:19,856 --> 00:07:20,857
Huh?

145
00:07:20,940 --> 00:07:21,941
You're not watching the movie?

146
00:07:22,484 --> 00:07:24,319
No, I think I should hurry back home.

147
00:07:24,819 --> 00:07:26,738
-Why?
-Should I just buy two tickets, then?

148
00:07:26,821 --> 00:07:28,573
Yeah, buy two. Just for you and Minjae.

149
00:07:28,657 --> 00:07:31,117
-Okay. Two tickets.
-No, wait. Wait, Youjin.

150
00:07:32,118 --> 00:07:33,119
I'll get the tickets, then.

151
00:07:45,799 --> 00:07:48,134
[muttering] Her and her damn temper...

152
00:07:53,306 --> 00:07:54,808
I'll be waiting outside.

153
00:07:54,891 --> 00:07:57,227
Hey, go tell Youjin
to wait out front for a minute.

154
00:08:03,274 --> 00:08:05,318
Sejin, where's Youjin?

155
00:08:06,695 --> 00:08:08,154
She said she's going home and then left.

156
00:08:08,905 --> 00:08:09,906
She went home?

157
00:08:11,533 --> 00:08:13,201
-There's Lim Youjin.
-Where?

158
00:08:13,785 --> 00:08:15,537
-The bus. On the bus.
-On the bus? On it?

159
00:08:16,287 --> 00:08:17,288
I don't see her.

160
00:08:19,332 --> 00:08:21,418
-Now, she's really gone.
-Jeez.

161
00:08:23,211 --> 00:08:24,713
That rude brat.

162
00:08:24,796 --> 00:08:27,132
I waved goodbye to her,
and she gave me the finger.

163
00:08:49,988 --> 00:08:51,990
What should we have for dinner
after the movie?

164
00:08:53,116 --> 00:08:54,117
Korean?

165
00:08:54,701 --> 00:08:55,702
Chinese?

166
00:08:56,202 --> 00:08:58,121
Japanese? Western?

167
00:08:58,705 --> 00:08:59,706
What would you like?

168
00:09:01,833 --> 00:09:03,543
Sejin, I'm really sorry.

169
00:09:05,754 --> 00:09:07,422
But can we see the movie another time?

170
00:09:10,133 --> 00:09:12,969
Well, I've been running around all day
for the wedding, and...

171
00:09:14,429 --> 00:09:15,430
I'm a little tired.

172
00:09:20,852 --> 00:09:21,853
Minjae.

173
00:09:23,938 --> 00:09:25,440
Is your leg bothering you that much?

174
00:09:27,400 --> 00:09:28,735
No, it's just...

175
00:09:31,821 --> 00:09:33,031
Let's see it another time.

176
00:09:45,835 --> 00:09:47,295
[Minjae] <i>Did you get home okay?</i>

177
00:09:51,800 --> 00:09:53,218
[quietly] Why isn't she replying?

178
00:10:18,034 --> 00:10:19,244
-[phone vibrating]
-Mmm?

179
00:10:20,203 --> 00:10:23,206
-[phone vibrating]

180
00:10:31,506 --> 00:10:32,507
Hello?

181
00:10:33,091 --> 00:10:34,759
What took you so long to pick up?

182
00:10:36,553 --> 00:10:38,054
You're brushing your teeth?

183
00:10:38,596 --> 00:10:40,306
Should we talk later, then?

184
00:10:40,390 --> 00:10:44,769
No, I can talk now. I can talk. I'm done.

185
00:10:49,190 --> 00:10:50,191
Did I see the movie?

186
00:10:52,485 --> 00:10:54,112
No, I didn't see the movie.

187
00:10:55,196 --> 00:10:57,407
Why would I watch a movie with Kim Sejin?

188
00:10:58,032 --> 00:10:59,659
That's why I just came home.

189
00:11:00,285 --> 00:11:01,286
I'm home now.

190
00:11:02,120 --> 00:11:03,121
I mean...

191
00:11:03,746 --> 00:11:06,708
You and Kim Sejin even bought tickets.
Why didn't you go?

192
00:11:07,208 --> 00:11:09,002
It sounded like a really fun movie.

193
00:11:09,085 --> 00:11:10,086
No, that was...

194
00:11:12,172 --> 00:11:15,008
He doesn't have any friends in Seoul,

195
00:11:15,842 --> 00:11:19,679
and the only people he knows
are us from the lab.

196
00:11:20,597 --> 00:11:22,724
We should at least look out for him.

197
00:11:23,892 --> 00:11:27,312
And since you guys are in the same cohort,
you should be nice to him too.

198
00:11:28,104 --> 00:11:31,149
Does Sejin really bother you that much?

199
00:11:31,232 --> 00:11:32,859
Do you get mad just looking at him?

200
00:11:32,942 --> 00:11:34,944
Well, it wasn't Kim Sejin...

201
00:11:36,321 --> 00:11:39,616
I wasn't mad at Kim Sejin.
I was mad at Park Minjae.

202
00:11:40,533 --> 00:11:42,118
Me? Why?

203
00:11:43,119 --> 00:11:45,246
I don't think you like me that much.

204
00:11:50,585 --> 00:11:51,586
<i>Are you still there?</i>

205
00:11:52,128 --> 00:11:53,129
Yeah.

206
00:11:53,630 --> 00:11:54,631
I'm here.

207
00:11:56,257 --> 00:11:59,594
You like me way less than I like you.

208
00:12:00,970 --> 00:12:02,180
Be honest with me.

209
00:12:03,890 --> 00:12:07,977
If Kim Sejin and I were both drowning,
who would you save first?

210
00:12:08,061 --> 00:12:09,062
What?

211
00:12:10,521 --> 00:12:11,731
[Youjin] <i>Why won't you answer?</i>

212
00:12:12,690 --> 00:12:14,525
<i>Who would you save, Kim Sejin or me?</i>

213
00:12:17,528 --> 00:12:20,073
That's just ridiculous.
I don't even know what to say.

214
00:12:21,449 --> 00:12:22,909
[Youjin] <i>Why is it ridiculous?</i>

215
00:12:22,992 --> 00:12:24,661
<i>I'm being totally serious.</i>

216
00:12:27,080 --> 00:12:29,374
Well, of course...

217
00:12:31,125 --> 00:12:32,502
I'd save you.

218
00:12:34,587 --> 00:12:37,840
Even if we both fell in,

219
00:12:38,841 --> 00:12:41,636
I'd be begging,
"Please save Youjin first."

220
00:12:44,931 --> 00:12:46,182
<i>Did you hear what I said?</i>

221
00:12:46,766 --> 00:12:48,268
Yeah, I'm listening.

222
00:12:50,603 --> 00:12:51,854
Then what if...

223
00:12:53,106 --> 00:12:57,318
our parents didn't approve of us
being together? What would you do, then?

224
00:13:01,864 --> 00:13:03,199
<i>Hello? Are you there?</i>

225
00:13:04,617 --> 00:13:05,618
[Minjae] Yeah.

226
00:13:07,954 --> 00:13:09,664
What would you do?

227
00:13:11,082 --> 00:13:12,583
[Youjin] <i>Well, I asked you first.</i>

228
00:13:13,293 --> 00:13:15,169
What would you do if they didn't approve?

229
00:13:15,878 --> 00:13:16,879
Well...

230
00:13:20,425 --> 00:13:23,720
Well, it's not like we're still minors.

231
00:13:28,850 --> 00:13:32,186
We don't have to do
everything our parents say, right?

232
00:13:32,270 --> 00:13:35,982
I think we can keep seeing each other
even if they disapprove.

233
00:13:36,774 --> 00:13:37,775
Hmm.

234
00:13:38,985 --> 00:13:40,611
[Minjae] <i>And what would you do?</i>

235
00:13:41,571 --> 00:13:42,947
If our parents disapproved?

236
00:13:43,948 --> 00:13:46,951
<i>Well, if your mom is against it,</i>

237
00:13:47,035 --> 00:13:48,828
<i>I think you should stop</i>
<i>seeing that person.</i>

238
00:13:49,579 --> 00:13:52,415
Who could possibly
be more important than your mom?

239
00:13:52,498 --> 00:13:56,044
She gave birth to you and raised you,
so she must have a good reason.

240
00:13:57,003 --> 00:13:58,588
I'd stop seeing you if my mom said so.

241
00:14:01,257 --> 00:14:02,258
<i>Are you listening?</i>

242
00:14:05,762 --> 00:14:08,389
Why does the connection keep cutting out?

243
00:14:11,976 --> 00:14:12,977
Oh.

244
00:14:15,229 --> 00:14:17,190
It must be because my battery is low.

245
00:14:20,109 --> 00:14:21,819
I've got to go now.

246
00:14:25,615 --> 00:14:26,616
Yeah.

247
00:14:27,450 --> 00:14:28,451
Okay.

248
00:14:29,160 --> 00:14:30,161
Bye.

249
00:15:13,996 --> 00:15:14,997
Are you asleep?

250
00:15:17,834 --> 00:15:18,835
Hey, are you asleep?

251
00:15:20,461 --> 00:15:23,089
Sejin, hey, wake up.
Go sleep at your place.

252
00:15:23,172 --> 00:15:24,549
-Huh?
-[Sejin groans]

253
00:15:25,466 --> 00:15:27,385
-You should go home.
-[Sejin] Ten more minutes.

254
00:15:28,136 --> 00:15:30,429
-What?
-[muttering] Ten more minutes...

255
00:15:31,764 --> 00:15:32,765
Ten...

256
00:15:47,947 --> 00:15:49,240
[quietly] Here, cover up.

257
00:16:10,553 --> 00:16:11,846
[Minjae yelling] Jesus Christ!

258
00:16:11,929 --> 00:16:13,973
Hey, you punk, get out of my bed!

259
00:16:14,557 --> 00:16:15,683
I said get out of my bed!

260
00:16:18,394 --> 00:16:19,729
For God's sake.

261
00:16:23,191 --> 00:16:24,192
Gosh.

262
00:16:24,692 --> 00:16:26,736
I must've done it in my sleep.

263
00:16:27,987 --> 00:16:30,865
I didn't even realize it. I was freezing.

264
00:16:30,948 --> 00:16:31,949
Fine.

265
00:16:34,619 --> 00:16:39,415
Come on, it was just between us guys.
You don't have to get so upset about it.

266
00:16:50,051 --> 00:16:52,553
Hey, there are plenty
of empty seats over there.

267
00:16:52,637 --> 00:16:54,096
-Let's sit together.
-Come on.

268
00:16:54,180 --> 00:16:55,556
[Subin] Hello.

269
00:16:56,474 --> 00:16:57,475
[Minjae] Hello.

270
00:16:58,059 --> 00:17:00,353
-Are you on your way to work?
-[Subin] Yes.

271
00:17:00,978 --> 00:17:01,979
Hello.

272
00:17:03,272 --> 00:17:04,273
Hello.

273
00:17:10,238 --> 00:17:12,240
BUS
COLLEGE OF ENGINEERING

274
00:17:27,255 --> 00:17:28,256
What are you doing?

275
00:17:30,925 --> 00:17:32,718
-Aren't you coming?
-Yeah.

276
00:17:34,845 --> 00:17:37,056
Did you forget something?
What were you staring at?

277
00:17:38,015 --> 00:17:39,267
I was just...

278
00:17:40,101 --> 00:17:43,020
checking to make sure
the bus was running okay.

279
00:17:43,104 --> 00:17:44,480
What are you saying?

280
00:17:46,774 --> 00:17:49,151
-Wait, do you...
-No.

281
00:17:49,777 --> 00:17:51,612
-You... [laughs]
-I don't like her.

282
00:17:51,696 --> 00:17:52,697
Jeez.

283
00:17:54,615 --> 00:17:57,034
I don't. I don't!

284
00:17:57,868 --> 00:17:59,328
They say birds of a feather
flock together.

285
00:17:59,954 --> 00:18:02,456
I can't believe she's Lim Youjin's friend.

286
00:18:02,540 --> 00:18:06,252
She may seem normal,
but I'm sure she'll turn out weird too.

287
00:18:06,335 --> 00:18:08,087
Come on. That can't be true.

288
00:18:09,338 --> 00:18:13,551
Also, Youjin can be
a little quirky and stubborn,

289
00:18:14,093 --> 00:18:15,928
but she's not weird or anything.

290
00:18:16,512 --> 00:18:17,597
She is.

291
00:18:17,680 --> 00:18:19,807
In fact, she's super weird.

292
00:18:20,391 --> 00:18:24,186
Okay, well... Enough about Youjin.
What else is bothering you?

293
00:18:26,606 --> 00:18:27,607
Her face.

294
00:18:29,233 --> 00:18:30,234
She's...

295
00:18:31,027 --> 00:18:33,154
Isn't she ridiculously pretty?

296
00:18:33,237 --> 00:18:34,363
What?

297
00:18:35,865 --> 00:18:39,493
I mean, she's almost
unrealistically beautiful.

298
00:18:39,577 --> 00:18:41,120
She doesn't even look like a real person.

299
00:18:41,704 --> 00:18:44,832
You almost start wondering
if she's a fairy or an angel.

300
00:18:45,708 --> 00:18:48,878
So she looks like
a fairy or an angel to you.

301
00:18:49,545 --> 00:18:51,756
Well, she's almost too beautiful,
you know?

302
00:18:52,715 --> 00:18:56,010
She's crossed the line.

303
00:18:58,512 --> 00:18:59,722
[laughing] Okay, I get it.

304
00:19:00,348 --> 00:19:02,308
So, what else is bothering you?

305
00:19:02,391 --> 00:19:06,228
It doesn't make sense
that someone like her is still single.

306
00:19:06,312 --> 00:19:10,566
She can basically date whoever she wants.
So why doesn't she have a boyfriend yet?

307
00:19:10,650 --> 00:19:13,027
Maybe she just hasn't met
the right person yet.

308
00:19:13,110 --> 00:19:14,403
That's a different matter.

309
00:19:14,487 --> 00:19:15,488
The right person...

310
00:19:18,074 --> 00:19:20,451
Am I the one she hasn't met yet?

311
00:19:20,534 --> 00:19:21,702
Do you think so too?

312
00:19:23,162 --> 00:19:24,705
Well, I don't know that.

313
00:19:25,289 --> 00:19:26,874
So why do you keep asking those questions?

314
00:19:27,833 --> 00:19:28,834
Well, I didn't.

315
00:19:30,711 --> 00:19:33,089
You brought it up first.

316
00:19:38,761 --> 00:19:39,887
Oh boy.

317
00:19:39,970 --> 00:19:43,933
If you want to ask her out,
you should give it a try, though.

318
00:19:44,600 --> 00:19:46,519
-Nah.
-Why not?

319
00:19:46,602 --> 00:19:47,728
I've got to study.

320
00:19:48,604 --> 00:19:51,107
Besides, I've never
really been into girls.

321
00:19:51,774 --> 00:19:52,775
What?

322
00:19:54,610 --> 00:19:57,113
It doesn't mean I'm into guys, though.

323
00:20:00,241 --> 00:20:01,242
I'm just busy.

324
00:20:02,034 --> 00:20:03,035
Okay.

325
00:20:03,536 --> 00:20:04,870
I need to study. Study.

326
00:20:04,954 --> 00:20:06,664
Sure. Suit yourself.

327
00:20:08,290 --> 00:20:12,837
The fan and actuator designs seem fine,
but we can't get the heat under control.

328
00:20:12,920 --> 00:20:15,297
Maybe the torque demand
in the motor is too high?

329
00:20:15,381 --> 00:20:16,424
[Taeho] Mmm.

330
00:20:16,507 --> 00:20:18,759
The battery is running a little hot too.

331
00:20:18,843 --> 00:20:20,720
Well, we'll have to rerun the simulation.

332
00:20:21,846 --> 00:20:25,766
We have to get the motor temperature
below 80 degrees, no matter what. Okay?

333
00:20:25,850 --> 00:20:28,519
So should we redesign the cooling system?

334
00:20:28,602 --> 00:20:30,646
If tweaking it doesn't work,
we'll have to.

335
00:20:33,524 --> 00:20:35,317
And...

336
00:20:35,818 --> 00:20:38,154
the control algorithm optimization.

337
00:20:38,654 --> 00:20:40,448
Youjin, do you want
to read up on it and try?

338
00:20:41,031 --> 00:20:43,117
-Hmm? Me?
-Yeah.

339
00:20:43,200 --> 00:20:46,036
But Lim Youjin doesn't know anything,
so how is she supposed to--

340
00:20:48,289 --> 00:20:49,290
Well...

341
00:20:50,082 --> 00:20:53,043
I've got the data downloaded, Ms. Lim.

342
00:20:54,336 --> 00:20:56,130
You can look it over and give it a try.

343
00:20:56,213 --> 00:20:59,717
Okay, good. If you run into any issues,
just ask Taeho or me.

344
00:20:59,800 --> 00:21:02,303
And take a look at Sejin's data too.

345
00:21:02,386 --> 00:21:04,138
-Okay.
-Good.

346
00:21:04,847 --> 00:21:06,223
-Let's wrap it up here.
-[Hangyeol] Okay.

347
00:21:06,307 --> 00:21:07,558
-Sure.
-[Taeho] All right.

348
00:21:10,811 --> 00:21:11,896
[Taeho] Gyeol. Chan.

349
00:21:11,979 --> 00:21:12,980
[Hangyeol and Chansoo] Yes?

350
00:21:13,063 --> 00:21:16,108
Let's go to the control room
for a quick check on the load torque.

351
00:21:16,192 --> 00:21:17,610
-[Hangyeol] Okay.
-[Taeho] Okay.

352
00:21:19,987 --> 00:21:22,114
-[Hangyeol] We'll be right back.
-[Minjae] Okay.

353
00:21:28,704 --> 00:21:29,705
Lim Youjin.

354
00:21:30,831 --> 00:21:31,957
What's up?

355
00:21:33,918 --> 00:21:36,629
I sent you an email, so give it a read.

356
00:21:36,712 --> 00:21:38,672
It's the paper I downloaded
from the archive

357
00:21:38,756 --> 00:21:42,426
and the comments I added
after reading it. Take a look.

358
00:21:43,302 --> 00:21:44,512
Okay.

359
00:21:45,221 --> 00:21:46,222
Well, thanks.

360
00:21:53,938 --> 00:21:57,149
Do you happen to have some time this week?

361
00:21:58,609 --> 00:21:59,693
Why?

362
00:21:59,777 --> 00:22:03,113
I was just wondering
if you wanted to grab a bite sometime.

363
00:22:04,281 --> 00:22:06,033
You and me? Why?

364
00:22:06,116 --> 00:22:07,243
What do you mean, why?

365
00:22:08,035 --> 00:22:09,495
We're in the same cohort,

366
00:22:10,788 --> 00:22:12,623
but we've been kind of distant.

367
00:22:12,706 --> 00:22:15,292
I thought we could change that
and get along. That's all.

368
00:22:20,589 --> 00:22:21,715
Oh.

369
00:22:21,799 --> 00:22:24,134
Yeah. Well, whatever. Okay.

370
00:22:29,098 --> 00:22:32,351
If just the two of us is awkward,
you can bring your friend too.

371
00:22:40,276 --> 00:22:41,610
Ah...

372
00:22:42,528 --> 00:22:44,697
Subin is my best friend.

373
00:22:45,698 --> 00:22:49,660
But how could I set her up
with that nutjob Kim Sejin?

374
00:22:49,743 --> 00:22:50,744
You think I'm crazy?

375
00:22:50,828 --> 00:22:52,997
You're not setting her up with him.

376
00:22:53,080 --> 00:22:55,833
It's just a casual meal. That's all.

377
00:22:55,916 --> 00:22:57,793
It's the same thing.

378
00:22:58,460 --> 00:23:00,421
You're basically asking my friend to...
What's it called?

379
00:23:01,005 --> 00:23:03,299
Right, jump on a grenade.

380
00:23:03,382 --> 00:23:05,301
You don't care
if the grenade kills my friend.

381
00:23:05,384 --> 00:23:07,303
Don't put it like that.

382
00:23:08,220 --> 00:23:09,221
Tell me.

383
00:23:10,139 --> 00:23:12,558
If Subin and I were drowning,
who would you save?

384
00:23:14,393 --> 00:23:15,978
I'd save my friend.

385
00:23:16,061 --> 00:23:17,271
I'd save Subin.

386
00:23:22,192 --> 00:23:23,193
You...

387
00:23:24,820 --> 00:23:26,572
I wasn't going to tell you this.

388
00:23:27,364 --> 00:23:29,617
I wasn't going to tell you this

389
00:23:29,700 --> 00:23:32,328
because I knew you'd go berserk
and want to kill Kim Sejin.

390
00:23:33,829 --> 00:23:35,664
Do you know what happened this morning?

391
00:23:36,373 --> 00:23:38,500
Why? What happened?

392
00:23:39,251 --> 00:23:42,129
Well, when I woke up
in the morning, Kim Sejin...

393
00:23:44,089 --> 00:23:45,841
was sleeping in my bed.

394
00:23:50,095 --> 00:23:53,098
I mean, he said he was going to sleep
in the living room.

395
00:23:53,182 --> 00:23:55,935
But when I woke up this morning,
the punk was lying next to me.

396
00:23:58,771 --> 00:24:00,731
What the...
Even I haven't slept in that bed yet.

397
00:24:00,814 --> 00:24:02,691
You have no idea how shocked I was.

398
00:24:03,275 --> 00:24:05,402
Did you get hurt anywhere?
Are you feeling okay?

399
00:24:05,486 --> 00:24:08,155
No, I didn't get hurt.

400
00:24:08,238 --> 00:24:09,239
But...

401
00:24:09,990 --> 00:24:11,367
it didn't feel good.

402
00:24:12,076 --> 00:24:14,536
Did Kim Sejin touch you?

403
00:24:14,620 --> 00:24:17,289
I have no idea. I was asleep.

404
00:24:17,373 --> 00:24:20,417
[sighs in exasperation] But you're mine!

405
00:24:20,501 --> 00:24:23,712
And you'd still save Subin over me?

406
00:24:26,131 --> 00:24:29,593
He just wants to grab a bite with her.
It's not a date or anything.

407
00:24:30,219 --> 00:24:34,974
After that, those two
can take it from there. Okay?

408
00:24:43,565 --> 00:24:45,651
Come on, you've seen him too.

409
00:24:46,235 --> 00:24:48,028
He's not bad-looking.

410
00:24:48,112 --> 00:24:49,822
He didn't seem like a total weirdo, right?

411
00:24:50,489 --> 00:24:53,617
It's just that I'm not really in a place
for that right now.

412
00:24:53,701 --> 00:24:55,494
And I'm not really looking to date.

413
00:24:55,577 --> 00:24:58,580
Subin, do me a favor
just this once. Please?

414
00:25:01,375 --> 00:25:05,337
If you really don't like him,
just stay for 10 minutes,

415
00:25:05,421 --> 00:25:08,257
then say you have a headache and go home.

416
00:25:09,049 --> 00:25:10,467
Wouldn't that be too rude?

417
00:25:10,551 --> 00:25:12,261
It's okay. It's not rude.

418
00:25:13,012 --> 00:25:16,306
Just stay for 10 minutes and leave. Okay?

419
00:25:16,390 --> 00:25:17,558
Hmm?

420
00:25:22,104 --> 00:25:23,105
Oh?

421
00:25:23,605 --> 00:25:24,606
-Here.
-Hey.

422
00:25:28,610 --> 00:25:30,029
-Here.
-[Minjae] Okay.

423
00:25:34,992 --> 00:25:35,993
Hello.

424
00:25:38,203 --> 00:25:39,329
-There.
-Please sit.

425
00:25:43,876 --> 00:25:46,795
So this is Jung Subin.

426
00:25:46,879 --> 00:25:49,506
And this is my lab mate, Kim Sejin,
who's in my cohort.

427
00:25:50,674 --> 00:25:51,675
Hello.

428
00:25:54,094 --> 00:25:58,098
Well, we met at the wedding, right?
We said "hi" then.

429
00:25:58,182 --> 00:26:00,684
Ah. Yeah, I remember.

430
00:26:00,768 --> 00:26:02,686
We said "hi" on the bus too. Both of us.

431
00:26:03,312 --> 00:26:04,313
Yes.

432
00:26:04,938 --> 00:26:06,940
Oh, so you've met a few times already.

433
00:26:07,024 --> 00:26:09,234
No need to feel awkward, then.

434
00:26:11,779 --> 00:26:13,280
-Here you go.
-Thank you.

435
00:26:13,363 --> 00:26:15,657
I hear everything is good,
so pick whatever you want.

436
00:26:17,159 --> 00:26:19,828
Yeah, it's Sejin's treat,
so go for the most expensive one.

437
00:26:19,912 --> 00:26:21,497
Yeah. Anything you like.

438
00:26:23,082 --> 00:26:24,833
[Subin] Hmm.

439
00:26:27,878 --> 00:26:29,922
-[mouthing] Not yet.
-[mouthing] Why?

440
00:26:33,759 --> 00:26:35,719
-By the way...
-Yes?

441
00:26:35,803 --> 00:26:38,430
Youjin and I have something to do.

442
00:26:39,306 --> 00:26:40,599
So I think we should get going.

443
00:26:42,434 --> 00:26:44,770
Why? Is it urgent?

444
00:26:44,853 --> 00:26:48,232
The professor asked us to do something,
so we should go to the campus.

445
00:26:49,608 --> 00:26:51,610
Well, I guess it can't be helped, then.

446
00:26:52,402 --> 00:26:55,989
Yeah, I guess you'll have to eat
without us today.

447
00:26:56,073 --> 00:26:58,826
Well, we can always
get together another time.

448
00:26:58,909 --> 00:27:00,869
We all know each other, anyway.

449
00:27:00,953 --> 00:27:02,162
Yeah.

450
00:27:02,246 --> 00:27:04,289
We can always get together again sometime.

451
00:27:04,373 --> 00:27:07,376
All right. Now, shall we?

452
00:27:07,960 --> 00:27:08,961
Sorry, guys.

453
00:27:11,839 --> 00:27:13,173
Come on. Let's go, Youjin.

454
00:27:14,842 --> 00:27:15,843
Let's go.

455
00:27:18,095 --> 00:27:20,097
-Okay, Minjae.
-No, don't get up.

456
00:27:21,515 --> 00:27:23,016
All right. Enjoy your meal.

457
00:27:23,100 --> 00:27:24,351
-Take care.
-Thanks.

458
00:27:32,860 --> 00:27:33,861
[softly] Let's go.

459
00:27:35,904 --> 00:27:37,030
What? Don't.

460
00:27:37,739 --> 00:27:40,158
Pick one. Do you want to save Subin or me?

461
00:27:41,368 --> 00:27:44,204
-I'll save Subin. I'll save her.
-Don't be like that. Come here.

462
00:28:12,190 --> 00:28:13,650
What would you like to have?

463
00:28:14,776 --> 00:28:15,777
Uh...

464
00:28:22,492 --> 00:28:24,244
I'm sorry...

465
00:28:25,495 --> 00:28:27,456
but I have a headache.

466
00:28:28,665 --> 00:28:30,542
I think I need to go back home.

467
00:28:33,295 --> 00:28:34,296
Oh...

468
00:28:37,633 --> 00:28:39,134
Is it really bad?

469
00:28:43,472 --> 00:28:46,433
Do you have a fever or anything like that?

470
00:28:46,516 --> 00:28:48,727
I don't have a fever.

471
00:28:49,519 --> 00:28:50,520
It's just a headache.

472
00:28:52,814 --> 00:28:55,734
Just sit here for a minute.
I saw a pharmacy on the way here.

473
00:28:55,817 --> 00:28:57,027
-I'll be right back.
-It's okay.

474
00:28:57,110 --> 00:28:58,236
I'll go get you some medicine.

475
00:28:58,946 --> 00:29:00,822
Please take it before you go.

476
00:29:00,906 --> 00:29:02,407
-No, I'm okay.
-I'll be real quick.

477
00:29:58,046 --> 00:29:59,047
Thank you.

478
00:30:00,716 --> 00:30:02,300
Goodbye. Hello.

479
00:30:02,384 --> 00:30:04,177
-Headache meds, please.
-For a headache?

480
00:30:05,345 --> 00:30:06,346
Uh...

481
00:30:07,097 --> 00:30:09,307
-Something that works fast...
-Yes.

482
00:30:10,100 --> 00:30:11,435
...and is gentle on the stomach.

483
00:30:11,518 --> 00:30:13,520
Sure. Got it.

484
00:30:14,146 --> 00:30:16,106
Something mild.

485
00:30:16,189 --> 00:30:17,399
Right, this one is mild.

486
00:30:31,621 --> 00:30:33,123
[panting] Here's some medicine
for your headache.

487
00:30:34,249 --> 00:30:35,375
You're all sweaty.

488
00:30:35,459 --> 00:30:38,211
How far did you go to get this?

489
00:30:39,463 --> 00:30:41,298
Not too far.
It was right around the corner.

490
00:30:41,882 --> 00:30:43,091
It only took a minute.

491
00:30:48,638 --> 00:30:49,639
Take it.

492
00:30:50,265 --> 00:30:52,059
Then you can head home.

493
00:30:55,979 --> 00:30:56,980
One tablet.

494
00:30:57,522 --> 00:30:58,523
One tablet?

495
00:31:10,619 --> 00:31:11,870
Would you like to order?

496
00:31:16,249 --> 00:31:18,085
We'll come back another time.

497
00:31:18,585 --> 00:31:19,753
I'm sorry.

498
00:31:19,836 --> 00:31:20,837
Oh...

499
00:31:28,386 --> 00:31:29,387
Let's go.

500
00:31:31,098 --> 00:31:32,099
Okay.

501
00:31:42,234 --> 00:31:43,235
Say "ah."

502
00:31:47,906 --> 00:31:48,907
What should we do now?

503
00:31:53,078 --> 00:31:54,287
How about a movie?

504
00:31:54,371 --> 00:31:55,497
-A movie?
-Yeah.

505
00:31:59,709 --> 00:32:00,877
It's too...

506
00:32:02,129 --> 00:32:03,130
crowded.

507
00:32:04,840 --> 00:32:07,509
Should we just watch a movie at home?

508
00:32:09,094 --> 00:32:11,221
Okay. But which movie?

509
00:32:11,805 --> 00:32:13,140
Is there anything you want to watch?

510
00:32:13,765 --> 00:32:14,766
Anything's fine.

511
00:32:17,310 --> 00:32:19,479
-Something sexy?
-Jeez...

512
00:32:20,522 --> 00:32:21,606
Why?

513
00:32:21,690 --> 00:32:23,316
Are you scared I might eat you alive?

514
00:32:24,192 --> 00:32:26,111
What do you mean, scared?

515
00:32:26,611 --> 00:32:27,904
Of course not.

516
00:32:28,780 --> 00:32:30,282
-[clears throat]
-You're cute.

517
00:32:33,326 --> 00:32:34,327
Hey.

518
00:32:34,911 --> 00:32:36,329
People are watching.

519
00:32:36,872 --> 00:32:38,123
-Don't do that.
-Why?

520
00:32:38,623 --> 00:32:41,459
Fine. Let's save that kiss
for when we get home, Minjae.

521
00:32:45,255 --> 00:32:48,884
I specifically asked for a mild one.

522
00:32:52,095 --> 00:32:55,390
You should go home and get some sleep.

523
00:32:56,433 --> 00:32:59,936
When you wake up,
you'll feel a lot better.

524
00:33:01,688 --> 00:33:02,689
Okay.

525
00:33:05,400 --> 00:33:08,820
Give it some time,
and if you still don't feel better,

526
00:33:08,904 --> 00:33:11,448
you should see a doctor.

527
00:33:14,743 --> 00:33:15,744
I'm sorry.

528
00:33:16,745 --> 00:33:17,746
What?

529
00:33:19,331 --> 00:33:20,332
Ah.

530
00:33:21,249 --> 00:33:22,459
Don't be.

531
00:33:22,542 --> 00:33:24,502
You're just sick.
There's no need to apologize.

532
00:33:26,463 --> 00:33:29,883
We can always grab a bite another time.

533
00:33:32,385 --> 00:33:33,386
It's okay.

534
00:33:35,889 --> 00:33:37,307
The taxi is here.

535
00:33:47,067 --> 00:33:48,068
Get in.

536
00:33:49,527 --> 00:33:52,280
-I'm sorry.
-You don't have to be. It's really okay.

537
00:33:53,573 --> 00:33:54,783
Well, let's make sure...

538
00:33:56,368 --> 00:33:57,369
we get a meal

539
00:33:58,161 --> 00:33:59,454
together next time.

540
00:33:59,537 --> 00:34:01,289
I'll treat you to something good.

541
00:34:01,373 --> 00:34:04,167
No. I'll treat you
to something even better.

542
00:34:07,462 --> 00:34:10,298
Sure, well... We can do that too.

543
00:34:10,382 --> 00:34:11,383
Mmm.

544
00:34:17,806 --> 00:34:18,848
Excuse me, sir.

545
00:34:18,932 --> 00:34:21,184
My friend is not feeling well,

546
00:34:21,268 --> 00:34:23,937
so please drive carefully.

547
00:34:24,020 --> 00:34:25,897
[driver] All right.
I'll get her home safely.

548
00:34:27,315 --> 00:34:28,733
Have a safe trip home.

549
00:35:34,591 --> 00:35:35,592
So?

550
00:35:35,675 --> 00:35:36,760
How did it go?

551
00:35:38,470 --> 00:35:40,597
She had a headache, so she just left--

552
00:35:40,680 --> 00:35:42,807
[mouthing] It's Sejin. Kim Sejin.

553
00:35:44,351 --> 00:35:45,352
Yeah.

554
00:35:45,935 --> 00:35:47,729
Yeah, she left.

555
00:35:52,567 --> 00:35:54,694
We can always grab a bite another time.

556
00:35:56,738 --> 00:35:57,739
It's fine.

557
00:35:58,239 --> 00:35:59,908
Yeah, things happen.

558
00:36:01,242 --> 00:36:02,869
But why did she suddenly get a headache?

559
00:36:05,038 --> 00:36:06,122
Okay.

560
00:36:06,206 --> 00:36:08,708
So she went home, and what about you?

561
00:36:09,459 --> 00:36:11,586
So I'm just by myself now.

562
00:36:12,128 --> 00:36:13,254
Where are you, Minjae?

563
00:36:13,338 --> 00:36:15,215
-Are you still nearby?
-Me?

564
00:36:15,757 --> 00:36:17,550
I'm not here.

565
00:36:17,634 --> 00:36:20,261
No, I mean, when I said, "I'm not here,"

566
00:36:20,929 --> 00:36:23,098
I'm already on my way home.

567
00:36:25,600 --> 00:36:26,851
Youjin?

568
00:36:27,644 --> 00:36:30,146
Youjin left too.

569
00:36:30,897 --> 00:36:33,858
-[mouthing] School. Say I went to school.
-School. She went to school.

570
00:36:33,942 --> 00:36:36,277
I think so.
She said she was going to school.

571
00:36:38,113 --> 00:36:39,489
[mouthing] Just hang up.

572
00:36:39,572 --> 00:36:40,740
Hang up.

573
00:36:40,824 --> 00:36:43,326
Hey, Sejin, I'm getting another call.
I've got to go.

574
00:36:43,410 --> 00:36:44,411
Okay.

575
00:36:44,911 --> 00:36:45,912
Well, then...

576
00:36:46,913 --> 00:36:49,207
I'll tell you more about it when we meet.

577
00:36:51,209 --> 00:36:52,210
Bye.

578
00:37:01,302 --> 00:37:03,138
So did you decide
what movie you want to watch?

579
00:37:03,805 --> 00:37:05,515
I told you, something sexy.

580
00:37:05,598 --> 00:37:08,435
-Come on.
-Oh, come on.

581
00:37:08,518 --> 00:37:11,104
-[phone vibrating]
-Why are you suddenly so into sexy movies?

582
00:37:12,397 --> 00:37:13,398
Oh...

583
00:37:13,481 --> 00:37:14,524
Who is it?

584
00:37:14,607 --> 00:37:15,608
It's Kim Sejin.

585
00:37:15,692 --> 00:37:16,985
I don't need to answer it.

586
00:37:17,944 --> 00:37:19,028
What should we watch?

587
00:37:19,612 --> 00:37:21,614
I don't know. I know nothing.

588
00:37:21,698 --> 00:37:23,241
[Youjin] You must like at least one movie.

589
00:37:23,324 --> 00:37:25,243
[Minjae] One movie... Then what about you?

590
00:37:52,771 --> 00:37:54,230
-[doorbell chiming]
-Huh?

591
00:37:55,607 --> 00:37:57,984
-That must be our <i>tteokbokki.</i>
-No, don't get up.

592
00:37:58,818 --> 00:37:59,944
I'll go get it.

593
00:38:03,364 --> 00:38:04,741
[softly] Jeez.

594
00:38:05,617 --> 00:38:07,577
What? What are you doing here?

595
00:38:07,660 --> 00:38:08,995
Hi, Minjae.

596
00:38:09,579 --> 00:38:10,705
You're home.

597
00:38:10,789 --> 00:38:12,290
Of course, I am. It's my home.

598
00:38:13,041 --> 00:38:14,459
Where else would I be?

599
00:38:15,668 --> 00:38:16,795
Well, it's just...

600
00:38:18,421 --> 00:38:21,174
I thought I'd give you
a detailed update on the blind date.

601
00:38:23,134 --> 00:38:24,385
And I need to tell you something.

602
00:38:24,469 --> 00:38:25,470
Okay.

603
00:38:26,638 --> 00:38:29,390
-I'll tell you inside.
-What? Inside where? No, say it here.

604
00:38:29,516 --> 00:38:31,559
Just say it here. Go ahead. What is it?

605
00:38:32,101 --> 00:38:33,102
It's a long story.

606
00:38:33,186 --> 00:38:34,354
Make it short, then.

607
00:38:35,355 --> 00:38:38,525
-Let's get inside and--
-Come on. Don't be like this. I'm busy.

608
00:38:38,608 --> 00:38:40,068
-[elevator dings]
-I have tons of work to do.

609
00:38:40,151 --> 00:38:41,402
Just hurry up and say it.

610
00:38:43,988 --> 00:38:45,698
Here's your volcano <i>tteokbokki.</i>

611
00:38:45,782 --> 00:38:47,492
[sighs] Oh.

612
00:38:51,204 --> 00:38:52,455
You ordered <i>tteokbokki?</i>

613
00:38:52,539 --> 00:38:53,748
For yourself?

614
00:38:53,832 --> 00:38:56,876
Yeah, I love <i>tteokbokki.</i>
I ordered it for myself. Why?

615
00:38:57,418 --> 00:38:58,503
What? What is it?

616
00:38:58,586 --> 00:38:59,963
Here, the <i>tteokbokki...</i>

617
00:39:00,046 --> 00:39:02,090
-That...
-You can give it to me. Thank you.

618
00:39:02,173 --> 00:39:04,259
For God's sake.

619
00:39:05,635 --> 00:39:06,636
Go.

620
00:39:10,348 --> 00:39:12,851
Yeah, give it to me. Okay.
Thank you. Give it to me.

621
00:39:12,934 --> 00:39:14,978
Give it to me and go. What are you doing?

622
00:39:15,061 --> 00:39:16,354
Can I have some <i>tteokbokki?</i>

623
00:39:16,437 --> 00:39:19,440
-Just go. Come on, give me that.
-I'm hungry too. Let's eat together.

624
00:39:20,108 --> 00:39:22,318
Order some with your own money!
Now give me that.

625
00:39:22,402 --> 00:39:24,779
Come on, let's eat together.
Food's better together.

626
00:39:24,863 --> 00:39:27,323
What do you mean, eat together?
No, get out. God!

627
00:39:27,407 --> 00:39:30,368
Seriously. For God's sake, jeez.

628
00:39:31,286 --> 00:39:33,746
Fine. Eat it and get out, okay?

629
00:39:36,207 --> 00:39:38,918
You just show up out of nowhere
and ask for my <i>tteokbokki?</i>

630
00:39:39,544 --> 00:39:40,545
Come on, give me that.

631
00:39:42,755 --> 00:39:45,258
Why haven't you eaten--
Hey, why are you going there?

632
00:39:45,341 --> 00:39:46,718
What? Why?

633
00:39:46,801 --> 00:39:47,969
What are you doing?

634
00:39:49,220 --> 00:39:50,471
What are you looking for?

635
00:39:50,555 --> 00:39:51,639
Huh?

636
00:39:52,724 --> 00:39:53,766
What are you doing?

637
00:39:55,810 --> 00:39:57,020
What's this about?

638
00:39:57,645 --> 00:39:58,855
-Well...
-Yeah.

639
00:40:00,481 --> 00:40:02,483
I thought I heard something.

640
00:40:03,526 --> 00:40:04,986
What are you talking about?

641
00:40:08,948 --> 00:40:10,825
-Now, get out.
-Was I just imagining it?

642
00:40:10,909 --> 00:40:13,661
Yes, you were. You were imagining it.
Now, get out. Go.

643
00:40:14,579 --> 00:40:17,790
Come here.
You said you were hungry. Let's eat.

644
00:40:17,874 --> 00:40:19,417
Where are you going now? Jeez.

645
00:40:19,918 --> 00:40:22,503
Why on earth are you doing this?
What is it?

646
00:40:23,087 --> 00:40:25,381
Tell me. I'll find it for you. What is it?

647
00:40:25,465 --> 00:40:26,591
-It's just...
-What?

648
00:40:27,216 --> 00:40:29,135
I think I hear something.

649
00:40:29,761 --> 00:40:31,262
It sounds like a person.

650
00:40:31,346 --> 00:40:34,057
What? There's no one here.
You're just hearing things.

651
00:40:34,140 --> 00:40:35,141
Exactly.

652
00:40:37,602 --> 00:40:38,603
It can't be...

653
00:40:40,313 --> 00:40:42,065
these guys talking, can it?

654
00:40:42,607 --> 00:40:44,984
-What are you talking...
-That'd be too creepy.

655
00:40:46,736 --> 00:40:48,196
Stop the nonsense and come here.

656
00:40:48,279 --> 00:40:50,448
-Wait.
-Why?

657
00:40:50,531 --> 00:40:52,408
See? I can hear it right now.

658
00:40:52,492 --> 00:40:53,826
I can hear a person talking...

659
00:40:55,244 --> 00:40:57,914
-and some music.
-All right, I hear it. Come here.

660
00:41:02,919 --> 00:41:05,672
You said you were hungry.
Hurry up and eat, then leave.

661
00:41:05,755 --> 00:41:06,756
I have a lot of things to do.

662
00:41:07,799 --> 00:41:09,217
Come on, eat up. Go on.

663
00:41:12,679 --> 00:41:13,680
What?

664
00:41:14,305 --> 00:41:15,348
Are you leaving?

665
00:41:18,017 --> 00:41:19,018
I need to use the bathroom.

666
00:41:19,102 --> 00:41:20,103
Go ahead.

667
00:41:24,857 --> 00:41:26,025
Hey, Sejin.

668
00:41:27,151 --> 00:41:28,569
Is this what you were hearing?

669
00:41:28,653 --> 00:41:29,904
-Huh?
-[increases volume]

670
00:41:30,655 --> 00:41:31,990
This? From my laptop?

671
00:41:32,699 --> 00:41:34,367
Ah...

672
00:41:35,743 --> 00:41:37,370
It was the movie.

673
00:41:37,453 --> 00:41:39,580
[Minjae] Yeah, this was the person
you were hearing.

674
00:42:01,019 --> 00:42:02,020
[whispering] Youjin.

675
00:42:02,103 --> 00:42:04,439
Youjin, are you okay?

676
00:42:04,522 --> 00:42:06,983
-[whispering] Can I go out?
-Come out now. Now.

677
00:42:10,862 --> 00:42:11,863
Right, Youjin.

678
00:42:13,072 --> 00:42:14,574
Your shoes are in the washing machine.

679
00:42:18,161 --> 00:42:19,203
Bye.

680
00:42:19,287 --> 00:42:20,288
Okay, bye.

681
00:42:20,371 --> 00:42:21,372
Call me.

682
00:42:21,456 --> 00:42:23,499
Hey, the door. Be careful.

683
00:42:27,545 --> 00:42:30,298
-[dishes clattering]
-[continues coughing]

684
00:42:31,924 --> 00:42:34,218
-Gosh, this keeps falling. [coughs]
-[door lock chimes]

685
00:43:04,540 --> 00:43:07,043
It's pretty spicy, isn't it?
The volcano one.

686
00:43:08,086 --> 00:43:10,421
The rice balls should help with the heat.
Have some.

687
00:43:12,548 --> 00:43:13,674
Aren't you going to eat?

688
00:43:13,758 --> 00:43:15,093
Me?

689
00:43:15,176 --> 00:43:17,095
I'll eat too, later.

690
00:43:21,224 --> 00:43:23,643
Right. So how did the blind date go?

691
00:43:25,561 --> 00:43:26,562
Hmm.

692
00:43:28,773 --> 00:43:29,941
Subin...

693
00:43:30,024 --> 00:43:31,025
Yeah.

694
00:43:31,109 --> 00:43:34,070
She suddenly said her head hurt.

695
00:43:34,946 --> 00:43:37,615
-A headache.
-Yeah, why did her head hurt?

696
00:43:39,325 --> 00:43:43,913
Sensitive, delicate women
tend to get headaches a lot.

697
00:43:43,996 --> 00:43:45,206
Low blood pressure, too.

698
00:43:46,249 --> 00:43:48,835
Man, you really do know everything,
don't you?

699
00:43:48,918 --> 00:43:50,628
I do know a lot of things.

700
00:43:55,258 --> 00:43:56,509
Well, anyway...

701
00:43:57,760 --> 00:43:59,095
She had a headache,

702
00:43:59,679 --> 00:44:01,055
so I got her some medicine.

703
00:44:01,764 --> 00:44:05,059
We said we'd grab a bite another time.

704
00:44:05,143 --> 00:44:06,310
Okay, good.

705
00:44:10,439 --> 00:44:12,024
But then...

706
00:44:12,859 --> 00:44:14,026
Yeah?

707
00:44:17,071 --> 00:44:18,781
After I saw Subin off...

708
00:44:21,951 --> 00:44:23,494
I saw something.

709
00:44:24,495 --> 00:44:26,205
What did you see? What was it?

710
00:44:36,048 --> 00:44:37,425
Nothing. [sighs]

711
00:44:42,513 --> 00:44:44,849
Hey, don't be so disappointed, okay?

712
00:44:44,932 --> 00:44:46,559
At least you've met her now.

713
00:44:47,143 --> 00:44:48,853
You can always see her again, right?

714
00:44:48,936 --> 00:44:51,022
You'll get another chance, Sejin.

715
00:44:56,027 --> 00:44:57,320
You're a pretty great guy.

716
00:44:57,403 --> 00:45:00,364
You're good-looking, kind, smart,

717
00:45:01,324 --> 00:45:02,325
hardworking,

718
00:45:03,451 --> 00:45:04,952
and you've got
a great academic background.

719
00:45:06,787 --> 00:45:09,624
So don't rush things. Just take your time.

720
00:45:09,707 --> 00:45:13,502
If you're sincere with her
and keep treating her with kindness,

721
00:45:13,586 --> 00:45:16,339
she'll eventually see
what a great guy you are.

722
00:45:22,511 --> 00:45:23,763
-By the way...
-Yeah.

723
00:45:26,349 --> 00:45:30,853
Even if I treat her sincerely
with kindness,

724
00:45:31,562 --> 00:45:37,985
she can still deceive me,
betray me, and lie to me, right?

725
00:45:38,069 --> 00:45:39,070
What?

726
00:45:40,321 --> 00:45:41,322
I mean...

727
00:45:43,241 --> 00:45:46,452
People say you should
never trust anyone, you know.

728
00:45:47,745 --> 00:45:50,456
I don't know what that's got to do
with this, though.

729
00:45:51,791 --> 00:45:54,377
Well, by that logic, the Bible also says,

730
00:45:56,170 --> 00:45:59,173
"If someone strikes you on one cheek,
offer them the other."

731
00:45:59,257 --> 00:46:01,759
And the Buddha said,
"Always show compassion to others."

732
00:46:01,842 --> 00:46:04,428
There are good sayings like those, too.

733
00:46:06,264 --> 00:46:07,265
Yeah.

734
00:46:08,391 --> 00:46:09,809
There are, but still...

735
00:46:12,436 --> 00:46:15,731
So don't rush it.

736
00:46:15,815 --> 00:46:19,485
Just take things a little slower,
and don't put any pressure on her.

737
00:46:19,568 --> 00:46:22,488
If you do that, I think it'll work out.

738
00:46:27,118 --> 00:46:28,119
Gosh, it's spicy.

739
00:46:32,498 --> 00:46:34,542
-You should have some. [clears throat]
-Yeah, okay.

740
00:47:09,285 --> 00:47:10,494
He went to bed early.

741
00:47:13,456 --> 00:47:14,457
Maybe he's tired.

742
00:48:06,258 --> 00:48:09,720
ENGINEERING BUILDING 3

743
00:48:09,804 --> 00:48:10,888
[Chansoo] Minjae.

744
00:48:12,098 --> 00:48:15,684
I have plans today. Can I leave early?

745
00:48:15,768 --> 00:48:17,561
[Taeho] It's past 5:00, anyway.

746
00:48:17,645 --> 00:48:20,272
That's not even leaving early. Just go.

747
00:48:22,274 --> 00:48:23,317
[quietly] No?

748
00:48:24,151 --> 00:48:27,488
Well, if you're done, you can go.

749
00:48:29,782 --> 00:48:32,660
All right, thanks for your hard work
on the experiment today.

750
00:48:33,327 --> 00:48:34,954
-Let's get off early.
-[Taeho] Okay.

751
00:48:35,037 --> 00:48:37,415
-[Chansoo] Okay.
-Thank you.

752
00:48:39,875 --> 00:48:41,085
Let's go.

753
00:48:42,795 --> 00:48:43,796
[Youjin] Bye.

754
00:48:49,093 --> 00:48:50,094
Bye.

755
00:48:50,886 --> 00:48:51,887
Bye.

756
00:48:54,306 --> 00:48:55,558
Youjin, aren't you going home?

757
00:48:56,725 --> 00:48:59,603
I need to organize the data I got
before I leave.

758
00:48:59,687 --> 00:49:01,313
I see. And you, Sejin?

759
00:49:01,397 --> 00:49:03,107
Yeah, I also have some work to finish.

760
00:49:03,190 --> 00:49:05,651
Yeah? Don't stay too late. I'll get going.

761
00:49:06,235 --> 00:49:07,862
-Bye.
-Bye.

762
00:49:17,621 --> 00:49:18,622
Lim Youjin.

763
00:49:19,248 --> 00:49:20,249
What?

764
00:49:20,875 --> 00:49:23,127
Do you have a lot of work?
When will you be done?

765
00:49:23,210 --> 00:49:24,837
Why do you ask when I'll be done?

766
00:49:25,421 --> 00:49:27,173
We said we'd grab a bite together,
remember?

767
00:49:29,133 --> 00:49:30,509
I have something to tell you too.

768
00:49:31,635 --> 00:49:33,053
What is it?

769
00:50:04,376 --> 00:50:05,711
What is it that you wanted to tell me?

770
00:50:09,465 --> 00:50:10,716
You said you'd tell me after the meal.

771
00:50:11,759 --> 00:50:13,052
We're done now, so shoot.

772
00:50:16,347 --> 00:50:17,473
I saw everything.

773
00:50:18,224 --> 00:50:20,184
You and Minjae are walking hand in hand.

774
00:50:25,731 --> 00:50:26,732
Are you two dating?

775
00:50:28,400 --> 00:50:30,277
No, we're not.

776
00:50:31,070 --> 00:50:32,738
Then why were you holding hands?

777
00:50:35,157 --> 00:50:36,242
Could it be...

778
00:50:37,535 --> 00:50:39,203
that you were mistaken?

779
00:50:41,330 --> 00:50:43,415
And even if I'm dating him,

780
00:50:43,916 --> 00:50:45,543
it's not something I have to tell you.

781
00:50:47,670 --> 00:50:50,089
Or why don't you ask Minjae yourself?

782
00:50:50,172 --> 00:50:53,342
Actually, I was going
to ask Minjae about it.

783
00:50:56,011 --> 00:50:57,972
And do you know what he said?

784
00:51:01,433 --> 00:51:02,560
What did he say?

785
00:51:04,061 --> 00:51:05,062
That if...

786
00:51:06,689 --> 00:51:09,900
you're sincere with someone
and treat them with kindness,

787
00:51:09,984 --> 00:51:12,570
they'll eventually see it.

788
00:51:15,114 --> 00:51:16,115
What?

789
00:51:17,408 --> 00:51:22,037
That's how naive and innocent he is.

790
00:51:24,039 --> 00:51:26,709
He has no idea that the world
doesn't work that way.

791
00:51:27,710 --> 00:51:30,421
He's kind and principled,
but he's completely clueless.

792
00:51:30,504 --> 00:51:33,924
He's nothing like you.

793
00:51:42,141 --> 00:51:46,645
I don't know why you're trying
to get close with Minjae.

794
00:51:49,648 --> 00:51:52,192
Actually, I do.

795
00:51:53,277 --> 00:51:56,196
But seriously, stop that.
You really can't do that.

796
00:51:58,991 --> 00:52:02,077
-What do you mean? I can't do what?
-Well, obviously...

797
00:52:05,581 --> 00:52:07,541
Stay away from Minjae from now on.

798
00:52:11,629 --> 00:52:14,006
Let's be honest. You're just using him.

799
00:52:14,089 --> 00:52:16,091
What does he have
that I could possibly use?

800
00:52:16,175 --> 00:52:18,135
Power. His power.

801
00:52:18,218 --> 00:52:22,222
What freaking power does he have?
He can't even get me out of work early.

802
00:52:22,306 --> 00:52:24,224
He's our lab lead, after all.

803
00:52:24,308 --> 00:52:27,853
He could give you the best projects
and special guidance on your papers.

804
00:52:27,936 --> 00:52:28,979
Something like that.

805
00:52:29,063 --> 00:52:31,065
Wow, I'm just speechless.

806
00:52:32,524 --> 00:52:34,735
Now that I know what's going on,
you've got to end it.

807
00:52:36,487 --> 00:52:37,655
Let Minjae go.

808
00:52:38,947 --> 00:52:42,826
He's not someone you can look down on
and use for your own benefit like that.

809
00:52:45,579 --> 00:52:46,955
I know I'm overstepping,

810
00:52:47,539 --> 00:52:50,626
and I'm not usually one to stick my nose
in other people's business.

811
00:52:51,335 --> 00:52:54,380
But this time, I have to step in.
That's why I'm telling you this.

812
00:52:55,714 --> 00:52:57,132
Gosh, my head hurts.

813
00:52:57,216 --> 00:52:58,467
Ah...

814
00:52:58,550 --> 00:53:00,052
I'll be honest with you.

815
00:53:00,678 --> 00:53:02,304
I don't have many friends,

816
00:53:03,055 --> 00:53:05,808
and there aren't many people
I genuinely like.

817
00:53:07,309 --> 00:53:09,645
But Minjae...

818
00:53:12,272 --> 00:53:13,273
I like him quite a lot.

819
00:53:13,357 --> 00:53:14,483
What?

820
00:53:14,566 --> 00:53:16,694
I mean, I like him as a person.

821
00:53:16,777 --> 00:53:17,986
I admire him.

822
00:53:20,072 --> 00:53:22,991
I can't just watch
while someone as shameless, sly,

823
00:53:23,075 --> 00:53:26,578
and mean as you walks all over him.
So end it now.

824
00:53:31,375 --> 00:53:33,127
I don't care whether you watch or not.

825
00:53:33,711 --> 00:53:34,712
I've got to go.

826
00:53:34,795 --> 00:53:36,422
So I've got a proposal for you.

827
00:53:37,256 --> 00:53:38,257
Let's call it...

828
00:53:39,133 --> 00:53:41,593
a challenge to a duel.

829
00:53:41,677 --> 00:53:43,512
Duels are supposed to be fought with guns.

830
00:53:45,013 --> 00:53:48,308
Lucky for you, guns are illegal
in this country, Kim Sejin.

831
00:53:48,892 --> 00:53:51,019
Whoever wins
gets to do whatever they want.

832
00:53:52,062 --> 00:53:55,649
If I win, you stay away from Minjae.

833
00:53:56,817 --> 00:53:57,818
And if you win...

834
00:54:01,321 --> 00:54:02,823
I'll quit the lab,

835
00:54:04,408 --> 00:54:05,617
and go back to Daejeon.

836
00:54:09,079 --> 00:54:11,165
You choose what we compete in.

837
00:54:11,248 --> 00:54:13,125
What... <i>FIFA?</i>

838
00:54:15,002 --> 00:54:16,003
<i>StarCraft?</i>

839
00:54:16,587 --> 00:54:17,588
<i>League of Legends?</i>

840
00:54:18,213 --> 00:54:19,590
Anything you're good at.

841
00:54:20,841 --> 00:54:22,384
It doesn't have to be a video game.

842
00:54:22,468 --> 00:54:25,971
We could solve math problems,
memorize words, or things like that.

843
00:54:26,889 --> 00:54:30,392
I'm even fine with a drinking game.

844
00:54:31,852 --> 00:54:35,773
Pick anything you're confident in,
anything you think you can beat me at.

845
00:54:37,691 --> 00:54:41,069
But we're not telling Minjae
or anyone else.

846
00:54:41,862 --> 00:54:42,863
What do you say?

847
00:54:45,449 --> 00:54:47,409
They'd think I'm crazy if I told them.

848
00:54:48,702 --> 00:54:49,703
Hey.

849
00:54:50,787 --> 00:54:53,874
I should've recorded all that
and played it for Minjae.

850
00:54:54,583 --> 00:54:55,584
Too bad.

851
00:54:56,668 --> 00:54:57,669
Are you not in?

852
00:54:58,545 --> 00:54:59,546
I'm heading out.

853
00:55:15,854 --> 00:55:17,481
What a nut. An absolute nutjob.

854
00:55:18,273 --> 00:55:19,900
What the hell is wrong with him?

855
00:55:19,983 --> 00:55:20,984
Jeez.

856
00:55:48,637 --> 00:55:50,389
Hi, I'd like to pay the check.

857
00:55:50,973 --> 00:55:52,391
Your total is 22,000 won.

858
00:56:03,110 --> 00:56:05,487
Here. Thank you. Goodbye.

859
00:56:05,571 --> 00:56:06,572
Bye.

860
00:56:13,453 --> 00:56:14,955
Hey, Kim Sejin.

861
00:56:20,919 --> 00:56:22,296
Can you really promise?

862
00:56:22,838 --> 00:56:23,839
What?

863
00:56:24,381 --> 00:56:26,341
If you lose, you'll go back to Daejeon.

864
00:56:27,259 --> 00:56:29,177
Yeah, if I lose.

865
00:56:29,261 --> 00:56:32,681
But if you lose, you get lost.

866
00:56:35,559 --> 00:56:38,478
You pick the game.
I don't care what we play.

867
00:56:39,479 --> 00:56:41,440
You don't care what we play?

868
00:56:41,523 --> 00:56:43,317
No, I don't.

869
00:56:43,400 --> 00:56:46,612
I'm going to beat you purely on skill.

870
00:56:48,572 --> 00:56:50,657
I never told you
because I didn't want to brag,

871
00:56:51,366 --> 00:56:55,787
but my IQ is 180.
That's way higher than your height.

872
00:56:57,122 --> 00:56:59,082
My IQ is 188.

873
00:56:59,166 --> 00:57:01,168
That's way higher than your height.

874
00:57:01,793 --> 00:57:02,794
That's your IQ?

875
00:57:02,878 --> 00:57:04,087
Why? Do you think I'm lying?

876
00:57:04,171 --> 00:57:07,049
An IQ of 180 or higher
is extremely rare worldwide.

877
00:57:07,132 --> 00:57:09,509
Only 0.003% of people have that.

878
00:57:09,593 --> 00:57:12,095
Yeah, that number sounds about right.

879
00:57:13,722 --> 00:57:15,891
It's like rolling
a six-sided die five times

880
00:57:15,974 --> 00:57:18,226
and getting the same number every time.

881
00:57:22,939 --> 00:57:24,775
0.003...

882
00:57:25,400 --> 00:57:27,194
Yeah, it's the same.

883
00:57:27,736 --> 00:57:28,737
It's...

884
00:57:29,655 --> 00:57:33,367
also the same as the odds of being dealt
a royal straight flush in poker.

885
00:57:34,493 --> 00:57:36,870
Yeah, I'm good at math too.

886
00:57:40,332 --> 00:57:41,500
Do you know how to play poker?

887
00:57:44,461 --> 00:57:45,921
It's not that hard a game, is it?

888
00:57:46,963 --> 00:57:48,006
We'll play just one hand.

889
00:57:50,384 --> 00:57:52,094
And we'll keep this a secret from Minjae.

890
00:57:52,177 --> 00:57:55,514
The moment you tell him, you lose.

891
00:58:45,522 --> 00:58:46,857
Hello?

892
00:58:46,940 --> 00:58:47,941
Minjae.

893
00:59:14,885 --> 00:59:16,219
-[line ringing]
-[phone vibrating]

894
00:59:21,099 --> 00:59:24,895
Hey, I'm sorry,
but I don't think I can come out.

895
00:59:27,606 --> 00:59:29,357
You should've given me a heads-up.

896
00:59:29,441 --> 00:59:31,651
You can't just show up
because you missed me.

897
00:59:31,735 --> 00:59:34,404
I was just...

898
00:59:38,074 --> 00:59:39,785
I'll see you at school, then.

899
00:59:40,827 --> 00:59:41,828
Okay.

900
01:00:03,809 --> 01:00:05,060
-Boo!
-You scared me.

901
01:00:05,560 --> 01:00:06,561
I got you.

902
01:00:07,354 --> 01:00:08,772
I was just messing with you.

903
01:00:16,696 --> 01:00:18,573
Sorry, I kept you waiting.

904
01:01:18,258 --> 01:01:22,178
BETWEEN STEPS

905
01:01:22,262 --> 01:01:24,556
<i>Professor, do you know how to play poker?</i>

906
01:01:24,639 --> 01:01:26,182
How did you do that?

907
01:01:26,266 --> 01:01:27,559
Anyway, I'm staying here.

908
01:01:27,642 --> 01:01:29,811
I hear it's a really good opportunity.

909
01:01:29,895 --> 01:01:31,813
If you like her, you should let her go.

910
01:01:31,897 --> 01:01:33,857
I'll never give up on Youjin.

911
01:01:33,940 --> 01:01:35,358
[Youjin] <i>Anything else besides luck?</i>

912
01:01:35,442 --> 01:01:37,360
<i>-</i>[Jihoon] <i>Mind games?</i>
-Hello.

913
01:01:37,444 --> 01:01:40,113
[Sejin] <i>Lim Youjin, are you really</i>
<i>going to play dirty like this?</i>

914
01:01:40,196 --> 01:01:41,281
We're going all in.

915
01:01:41,364 --> 01:01:43,700
What the... Those punks.

916
01:01:43,783 --> 01:01:46,119
If you don't open this door
before I count to three,

917
01:01:46,202 --> 01:01:48,204
<i>you guys are going to be</i>
<i>in serious trouble.</i>

918
01:01:48,288 --> 01:01:49,289
Hey! [shushes]
